# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
# Every value here is referenced by name only in CLAUDE.md. Placeholders below
# are intentionally fake.
#
# Format: KEY=value, no spaces around `=`. Quotes are optional and usually
# unnecessary — WxCC/Webex tokens and secrets are base64-ish (letters, digits,
# -, _, and = padding) and need no quoting. Only wrap a value in single quotes
# if it contains a space or a `#` (an unquoted ` #` starts an inline comment and
# would truncate the value).

# ---- WxCC Service App (OAuth, server-to-server) ----
# Created in the Webex developer portal, authorized in Control Hub, scopes:
# cjp:task_write and cjp:task_read.
WXCC_SERVICE_APP_CLIENT_ID=changeme-client-id
WXCC_SERVICE_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=changeme-client-secret
# Bootstrap tokens generated when the Service App is first authorized. The access
# token lasts ~14 days; the token manager auto-refreshes it via the refresh token
# (~90 days) against https://webexapis.com/v1/access_token. See
# docs/webex-service-app-auth.md. NOTE: runtime-refreshed tokens are held in memory
# for now — these two values only seed the process at boot.
WXCC_SERVICE_APP_ACCESS_TOKEN=changeme-access-token
WXCC_SERVICE_APP_REFRESH_TOKEN=changeme-refresh-token

# WxCC organization ID that authorized the Service App.
WXCC_ORG_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# WxCC Tasks API base URL — REGION/DATA-CENTER SPECIFIC. Must match your org's DC:
# https://api.wxcc-{dc}.cisco.com where dc is one of us1|eu1|eu2|ca1|jp1|sg1|anz1.
# There is no universal default; the value below is a placeholder for the US DC.
WXCC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.wxcc-us1.cisco.com

# Business address configured on the Custom Messaging asset in Control Hub. Sent as
# Create Task's destination.id — the task fails (CHANNEL_ASSET_UNDEFINED) if it's wrong.
WXCC_BUSINESS_ADDRESS=webex-messaging

# ---- WxCC Custom Messaging asset (outbound webhook side) ----
# Secret configured on the Custom Messaging asset in Control Hub. Verifies EVERY
# request on /webhooks/wxcc: HMAC-SHA256 over the raw body vs. the X-WebexCC-Signature
# header. That one route receives both the asset-level outbound webhook AND the
# task-lifecycle Subscriptions API webhooks — so any subscription you create by hand
# (Postman/Bruno/script; this app has no Subscriptions client) MUST use this same
# value as its `secret` and this same URL. A different or missing secret => 401.
# See docs/wxcc-webhooks-cc.md → "Provisioning subscriptions". (Distinct scheme from
# the Webex Messaging secret below — HMAC-SHA1 — never interchange them.)
WXCC_ASSET_WEBHOOK_SECRET=changeme-wxcc-asset-webhook-secret

# Name of the Custom Messaging channel as configured in Control Hub. Must match
# the ChannelAdapter.channelId of the adapter that owns it (see channel-adapter.ts).
# This is config, not a secret, but it lives here so all channel wiring is in one place.
WEBEX_MESSAGING_CHANNEL_NAME=webex-messaging

# ---- Webex Messaging (inbound customer side) ----
# Bot access token used to (a) create the messages webhook and (b) fetch decrypted
# message text via GET /v1/messages/{id} (webhook payloads omit the text).
WEBEX_BOT_TOKEN=changeme-webex-bot-token
# Secret supplied when creating the Webex Messaging webhook; used to verify the
# X-Spark-Signature HMAC-SHA1 header on inbound notifications.
WEBEX_MESSAGING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=changeme-webex-messaging-webhook-secret

# ---- Server ----
# Cloud Run injects PORT at runtime; 8080 is the local/default fallback.
PORT=8080

# This process's own public HTTPS URL, no trailing slash — the Cloudflare Tunnel
# host in local dev, the Cloud Run URL in production. Used only by LocalFileRelay
# (src/core/files/) to build attachment URLs under /files/:id that WxCC and the
# channel platform can retrieve unauthenticated. Must be the SAME host you
# registered as the webhook URLs above — not a separate domain.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://changeme.trycloudflare.com
